          "id": 2,
          "options": {
            "content": "**Purpose.** Health of the event pipeline every journey depends on: service outbox \u2192 Debezium (CDC) \u2192 Kafka \u2192 purekafka consumers.\n\n**Use it when** the Dispatch & async flow dashboard shows event age or lag rising, or a service's Kafka consumers are failing.\n\n**How to read it**\n- Producers & consumers: DLQ publishes and stream restarts are failures. Retries and breaker opens show a dependency struggling.\n- Broker: group lag rising while the write rate is flat means consumers can't keep up.\n- Connect & Debezium: connectors and tasks should be RUNNING and Debezium connected. Behind source is the outbox delay.\n\n**Background:** [USE method (best practices)](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/latest/dashboards/build-dashboards/best-practices/) \u00b7 [Hierarchy of needs](https://grafana.com/docs/learning-hub/intro-to-grafana-cloud/00-intro/02-hierarchy-of-needs) \u00b7 [Microservice monitoring](https://www.sysdig.com/blog/microservice-monitoring)",
            "mode": "markdown"
          },
          "repeatDirection": "h",
          "title": "",
          "transparent": false,
          "type": "text"
        }
      ],
      "title": "About this dashboard",
      "type": "row"
    },
